1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,639
Confide  settles  tokenized  stock

2
00:00:02,639 --> 00:00:04,440
against  a  stablecoin  in  a  single

3
00:00:04,440 --> 00:00:06,399
transaction  and  neither  side

4
00:00:06,399 --> 00:00:07,840
publishes  what  moved.

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,520
Delivery  and  payment  in  one

6
00:00:10,520 --> 00:00:12,640
transaction  and  the  only  people

7
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:14,319
who  can  read  either  number  are

8
00:00:14,319 --> 00:00:16,280
the  two  making  the  trade.

9
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:17,719
Neither  side  could  have  happened

10
00:00:17,719 --> 00:00:19,360
without  the  other,  which  is  the

11
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,840
only  thing  a  clearing  house  is

12
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:23,559
for  and  there  isn't  one.

13
00:00:23,559 --> 00:00:26,160
Confide  holds  nobody's  assets  and

14
00:00:26,160 --> 00:00:28,200
stands  between  nobody.

15
00:00:28,201 --> 00:00:30,801
So,  why  hide  it?  If  you  hold

16
00:00:30,801 --> 00:00:32,881
tokenized  stocks  on  Solana,

17
00:00:32,881 --> 00:00:34,881
everyone  can  see  what  you  hold.

18
00:00:34,881 --> 00:00:37,161
Nobody  attacked  anything.  The  chain

19
00:00:37,161 --> 00:00:39,161
simply  publishes  it,  the  moment

20
00:00:39,161 --> 00:00:40,681
each  purchase  settles.

21
00:00:40,962 --> 00:00:43,601
This  is  a  real  account  on  Solana.

22
00:00:43,601 --> 00:00:45,642
Right  now,  the  chain  says  it

23
00:00:45,642 --> 00:00:49,762
holds  nothing.  It  holds  173,000

24
00:00:49,762 --> 00:00:50,682
shares.

25
00:00:50,683 --> 00:00:53,523
Nearly  2,000  of  them,  from  three

26
00:00:53,523 --> 00:00:55,203
issuers  with  nothing  to  do  with

27
00:00:55,203 --> 00:00:57,363
each  other.  Every one  leaves  the

28
00:00:57,363 --> 00:00:59,603
auditor  key  empty,  and  every one

29
00:00:59,603 --> 00:01:01,483
needs  the  issuer's  signature  to  open

30
00:01:01,483 --> 00:01:02,403
an  account.

31
00:01:02,404 --> 00:01:04,844
So,  I  stopped  reading  the  settings

32
00:01:04,844 --> 00:01:06,244
and  counted.

33
00:01:06,244 --> 00:01:08,763
three hundred and twenty-nine thousand

34
00:01:08,763 --> 00:01:11,444
accounts  across  Apple,  NVIDIA,

35
00:01:11,444 --> 00:01:14,163
SpaceX  and  Anthropic.

36
00:01:14,163 --> 00:01:15,444
Not  one.

37
00:01:15,685 --> 00:01:17,965
That  dollar  has  the  same  empty

38
00:01:17,965 --> 00:01:20,325
auditor  slot  and  the  same  locked

39
00:01:20,325 --> 00:01:23,125
door.  Two  regulated  issuers,  two

40
00:01:23,125 --> 00:01:25,525
different  asset  classes,  the  same

41
00:01:25,525 --> 00:01:28,084
dead  end.  This  was  never  a  story

42
00:01:28,084 --> 00:01:29,685
about  tokenized  stocks.

43
00:01:29,686 --> 00:01:32,286
You  cannot  do  this  on  one.  A

44
00:01:32,286 --> 00:01:34,326
pool's  reserves  are  public  and  a

45
00:01:34,326 --> 00:01:36,286
trade  moves  them  by  exactly  the

46
00:01:36,286 --> 00:01:38,486
amount  traded.  So  anything  settled

47
00:01:38,486 --> 00:01:40,926
against  a  pool  publishes  the  size,

48
00:01:40,926 --> 00:01:42,806
whatever  the  token  can  do.

49
00:01:42,806 --> 00:01:44,766
It  has  to  be  two  parties

50
00:01:44,766 --> 00:01:46,006
directly.

51
00:01:46,006 --> 00:01:47,766
That  is  not  a  gap  here.  It  is

52
00:01:47,766 --> 00:01:49,846
why  this  is  shaped  as  it  is.

53
00:01:49,847 --> 00:01:51,927
The  chain  will  not  assemble  that

54
00:01:51,927 --> 00:01:54,007
trade  for  you.  The  proofs  do  not

55
00:01:54,007 --> 00:01:55,767
fit  in  a  transaction  and  on  a

56
00:01:55,767 --> 00:01:57,567
mint  that  charges  a  fee,  one  of

57
00:01:57,567 --> 00:01:59,647
them  does  not  fit  at  all.

58
00:01:59,647 --> 00:02:01,687
Confide  builds  them,  puts  them  on

59
00:02:01,687 --> 00:02:03,606
chain  and  hands  each  side  the

60
00:02:03,606 --> 00:02:05,287
the other's  amount  to  decrypt  before

61
00:02:05,287 --> 00:02:06,287
signing.

62
00:02:06,287 --> 00:02:07,647
That  is  the  product.

63
00:02:07,648 --> 00:02:10,248
Nobody  outside  this  repository  has

64
00:02:10,248 --> 00:02:11,848
used  any  of  it.

65
00:02:11,848 --> 00:02:14,608
But  what  is  left  is  not  unknown.

66
00:02:14,608 --> 00:02:16,408
Each  obstacle  is  a  condition  you

67
00:02:16,408 --> 00:02:18,207
can  check.  And  for  the  two  that

68
00:02:18,207 --> 00:02:20,088
decide  the  market,  the  work  on

69
00:02:20,088 --> 00:02:22,288
the  far  side  is  already  running.

